## Catch regressions in CI with Gates and Verdicts


Evals don't have to live only in a dashboard. Run them in code to catch regressions in CI/CD before you ship.[Gates and Verdicts](https://mastra.ai/docs/evals/gates-and-verdicts) turn behavior checks and scorer thresholds into a pass/fail verdict your test suite can assert on.


```text
import   {   runEvals   }   from   '  @mastra/core/evals  '  ;


try   {
// Check your agent against your quality requirements
const   result   =   await   runEvals  ({
target: refundPolicyAgent,
data,
scorers: [{ scorer: refundCorrectnessScorer, threshold:   1   }],
});


console.  log  (  '  Refund check:  '  ,   result.verdict);
if   (result.verdict   !==   '  passed  '  )   {
process.exitCode   =   1  ;
}
}   catch   (error)   {
console.  error  (  '  Refund check could not complete:  '  ,   error);
process.exitCode   =   1  ;
}
```


Optionally turn this into a GitHub Action, so every pull request runs your evals automatically and shows the verdict as a check, helping you catch regressions before you merge.


